index 0000000..c814e77
--- /dev/null
+++ b/private/linux-native/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@
+# Private bc01 native acceptance prototype — UNVERIFIED
+
+Base: `a95976a`; private branch `test/linux-native-acceptance`.
+This is a test-only adaptation, not a supported public Linux sandbox framework.
+**No Linux execution or pass is claimed. Parent/operator review precedes execution.**
+Nothing here installs agents, accesses SSH/production/R2, or reads host agent
+configuration, credentials or package source. The host launcher reads only the
+explicit public inputs' metadata, `/proc/self/ns/{net,pid,mnt}` symlink identities,
+and its own newly created synthetic proof files. The operator stages packages;
+the launcher never binds a host home, including the home from which a public
+package was copied. Do not transfer home/config trees as "assets".
+
+## Required inputs (operator supplies; no discovery/download)
+
+- Linux bubblewrap with functional `--unshare-all`, fresh `--proc /proc`, minimal
+  `--dev /dev` PTYs, `--clearenv`, `--remount-ro /` and unprivileged execution.
+  The reported `/nix/store` `true` smoke test is a prerequisite, **not** evidence
+  that this acceptance or its preflight passed.
+- An existing **empty, owned 0700** run directory, and the reviewed private source
+  tree, outside that directory. Only `run/scratch` is mounted writable.
+- Explicitly staged **public** actual Claude Code **2.1.296**, Codex **0.162.0**,
+  Pi **1.2.0** packages and runtime closure under an owned assets directory.
+  Pass exact relative executable paths; do not replace them with mock CLIs or
+  version wrappers. Pi must retain its actual `.../pi-coding-agent/...` script
+  pathname and executable bit. Preserve its package dependencies and metadata.
+  Symlinks may reference only other staged assets or explicitly mounted public
+  runtime outputs; a symlink back into host home intentionally fails.
+- `assets/bin/{sh,env,script,stty,node,cc}`: public real runtime executables or
+  links into explicitly approved public closures. `script` must be util-linux.
+  `cc` plus its complete public compiler/linker closure is needed for `-race`.
+  Stage any further dependencies needed by the actual CLI distributions, too.
+- Exact public Go **1.27.2** toolchain directory (`go.mod` requires Go 1.27),
+  and an already-populated module cache matching `go.sum`, mounted read-only.
+  No network/module/toolchain download: `GOPROXY=off`, `GOSUMDB=off`,
+  `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, `GOENV=off`. Go's writable cache is fresh owned scratch.
+  `-buildvcs=false` prevents the private worktree's external `.git` pointer from
+  requiring any host repository access; no Git executable is needed inside.
+- Enumerate every approved public runtime closure output with `--runtime`.
+  Prefer individual `/nix/store/<hash>-<name>` roots, **not** all `/nix/store`.
+  Narrow system-library paths are accepted, but their loader aliases must also
+  be available inside the namespace: do not solve missing libraries by binding
+  the host root, `/usr`, `/bin`, `/etc`, `/proc` or a home. The template resolves
+  input symlinks. The bc-01-specific launcher provides Debian x86_64 `/lib` and
+  `/lib64` loader aliases into `/usr/lib`; the operator must bind the approved
+  public `/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu` library directory when staging its unchanged
+  Node/Claude ELF files. This is public runtime code, not host configuration.
+  Do not mount Nix outputs containing private material. No host agent source
+  or private SDK inspection is required or authorised.
+
+The template deliberately fails on incomplete closures, disabled IPv6 with a
+non-ENETUNREACH probe result, non-loopback interfaces/routes, protocol/flag
+changes, or version mismatch. Fix staging only; do not add an unsandboxed
+fallback. If trust/protocol/lifecycle differs, preserve evidence and **stop and
+report the gap**. In particular Codex 0.162.0 is not assumed equivalent to the
+Mac 0.162.1: scratch trust still uses the existing independently pinned identity
+fixtures, never the collector's trust implementation.
+
+## Review, then authorised Linux command template
+
+Paths below are placeholders for existing approved inputs, not host-discovery
+commands. `python3 -I -S` avoids Python user-site/environment startup behavior.
+Use an absolute public Python interpreter path on the authorised host.
+
+```sh
+/public/python3 -I -S /reviewed/source/private/linux-native/launch.py \
+  --bwrap /public/bwrap \
+  --run /owned/empty-run \
+  --source /reviewed/source \
+  --assets /owned/public-assets \
+  --modulecache /public/populated-modulecache \
+  --gotoolchain /public/go1.27.2 \
+  --claude packages/claude/claude \
+  --codex packages/codex/codex \
+  --pi packages/pi-coding-agent/dist/cli.js \
+  --runtime /nix/store/EXACT-public-runtime-output
+# Repeat --runtime for the complete approved public closure.
+```
+
+The outer launcher uses an empty inherited environment, bubblewrap clearenv and
+an explicit synthetic environment. It builds a read-only synthetic root, binds
+only the inputs above, supplies synthetic passwd/group, and mounts fresh proc
+for its new PID namespace. No host `/etc`, `/proc`, socket, home or credentials
+are exposed. All Go invocations, `TestMain`'s collector build, the fake server,
+real agents, observers and detached collectors run **inside that one outer
+NET/PID/mount namespace boundary**. No agent-level sandbox flag substitutes for
+this boundary; direct child execution inherits it without making a second netns.
+The existing Codex `--sandbox read-only` argument remains unchanged.
+
+The only invocation inside the outer offline shell is:
+
+```sh
+go test -race ./cmd/agent-sessions -run '^TestLiveAgents$' -count=1 -v
+```
+
+Before **any** agent (including `--version`), mandatory Go preflight:
+
+- Requires the private read-only manifest, and compares actual NET/PID/mount
+  identities to the host identities captured by the outer launcher. Verifies
+  `/proc/1/ns/pid` agrees with the inner PID namespace.
+- Requires only an active `lo`, loopback addresses and loopback-only routes
+  (Linux unreachable IPv6 default entries on `lo` are allowed).
+- Requires real HTTP loopback health and scratch write/readback success.
+- Requires numeric IPv4 `192.0.2.1` and IPv6 `2001:db8::1` TCP probes to return
+  kernel **ENETUNREACH**, not timeout, unavailable curl, proxy or DNS failure.
+- Attempts writes to existing read-only synthetic canary and manifest; requires
+  EROFS/permission and unchanged hashes. Requires the known owned synthetic
+  external canary (not mounted) to be unreadable; no actual host config is probed.
+- Repeats **all** controls in a real `setsid` descendant and requires it to retain
+  the exact same confined namespaces. The child exits in init before TestMain.
+
+**Linux permits namespace-local networking to any loopback port**, unlike the
+Mac sandbox's single exact-port rule. This is stated in the test log, not hidden
+behind a fake sandbox flag. There is no external network interface or route.
+
+The existing fake SSE server, observer, scratch installer and archive verifier
+are reused unchanged. Lifecycle still requires all three real events, assistant
+reply, actual ordered argv/time and byte-exact final source with no explicit
+sync/backfill. Interactive Claude/Codex preserve Stop/held-input/orderly-exit
+behavior; only `script` argument syntax changes to Linux
+`-q -e -f -c COMMAND /dev/null`. Pi loads only the existing generated extension.
+Version output is asserted exactly, not used to infer protocol compatibility.
+
+## Evidence / disposition
+
+`run/acceptance.log` contains the outer exit and full Go output, preflight
